{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785994109219179001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"rancid-vane-wreak","assignee":"","attestations":{"plan-review":{"algorithm":"HMAC-SHA256","author":"Iso Tester","head_sha":"3ebb6a5cf270e92f556a6391a033c1d0021a7dfa","key_id":"412fa5372ad877e0","kind":"plan-review","manifest":["plan-review: PASS","ticket: 9d34-bfcd-54c3-4e7a","material: d84164a5f87fc4bb","model: claude-sonnet-4-6","runner: pydantic_ai","blocking: 0","advisory: 9","regver: 83e5f63ad06d893a","verified-at-sha:9450d0462dd64818fdd7d99df3f6632352a9be1d","dep 2881cd22da78c182ef20311cd86af4c2ae282d34100cd08cca54dfc324be5e8f src/rebar/llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py","dep 24f33ee78c9dbb2b16b6b328e5543cbc1b9042f14657f2d78fe0e4e2c6dfcaa3 src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py","dep e908577724da9f61a8c0126cb75b72d41aa862f1c03ccd568b4fdcee54fa0edf src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py"],"signature":"d8e423c571bf3b2b5246d395357452a7506ab53a7a2b38476106943a9f98cf62","signed_at":1782694530721500000}},"author":"Iso Tester","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":7},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1782605234072316001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[],"description":"Each plan-review workflow op independently re-assembles the entire ticket graph from the store, so one gate run does ~4×(1 + 1 + K children) `show_ticket`/`list_tickets` reads. On an epic with many children this is the latency the observability commit (`08cd4c325`) was added to explain — \"a slow epic review looks like a hang\" — a client-facing reliability/perceived-performance issue.\n\n## Why\nThe B-RETIRE migration decomposed the review into pure `uses` ops but gave them no shared context, so each re-reads + re-derives the graph (`orchestrator.assemble_context` is itself an N+1 read: `show_ticket` + `list_tickets(parent=)` + one `show_ticket` per child).\n\n## What / files\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py:66,147,212,235` — the precheck/assemble/verify_inputs/coach_inputs ops each call `orchestrator.assemble_context(...)`.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py:85` and `__init__.py:108` — assemble again.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py:77-110` — `assemble_context` (the N+1 read).\nApproach: assemble `PlanContext` ONCE in `plan_review_precheck`, serialize its `state`/`children` into the precheck step outputs, and have downstream ops reconstruct `PlanContext` from those outputs (as `plan_review_coach` already does at `workflow_ops.py:342`). Alternatively memoize on `(run_id, ticket_id)`.\n\n## Scope\nIn: eliminate the redundant re-reads within one gate run; preserve verdict bytes exactly. Out: changing the verdict/finding shape or the workflow YAML's op sequence.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A single plan-review gate run assembles the ticket graph at most once (assert via the observability step counts / a read-counter spy).\n- [ ] Verdict output is byte-identical to pre-change for a fixed fixture (characterization test).\n- [ ] Measured store reads for an epic-with-K-children review drop from ~4×(2+K) to ~(2+K).\n- [ ] Existing plan-review tests pass.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py","reason":"assemble PlanContext once"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py","reason":"assemble_context N+1 read"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py","reason":"reuse assembled context"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","5ca8-5993-ca83-40f1"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"5ca8-5993-ca83-40f1","parent_status_uuid":"809c686c-e0c8-47f5-9c2e-00efedd29a46","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["audit-2026-06-27","oss-remediation"],"ticket_id":"9d34-bfcd-54c3-4e7a","ticket_type":"story","title":"Eliminate redundant ticket-graph re-assembly in plan-review gate","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6f88d3e6-13bd-46f4-87f7-b0e499f08533","3b543dc3-3ac1-419a-88b4-1b66ac97b12e","44078092-3810-4e90-853e-98c76b44b2b6","87f4cec4-7d36-483a-8929-46dea89229f4","809c686c-e0c8-47f5-9c2e-00efedd29a46","e33a3941-5cde-48ff-80d4-8d73240aaf65","e3538c00-dcb8-4bbb-9ca1-3cd977c73d5d","1c6a5ece-67f5-4b7e-80f5-4b9abdd5d523","857b3390-d8e3-4db9-a16c-ed081e5c32ca"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785994109219179001,"uuid":"b8b59d40-0442-4319-a47d-9597a512e9ff"}